# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate carries the time evolution $e^{-itH}$ of a whole operator. A fermion-to-fermion synthesis rewrites that gate into a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") of smaller fermionic gates. Both sides of the rewrite stay in fermionic space, which is what distinguishes it from the fermion-to-qubit synthesis that follows: the operator’s [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") (see [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)) survive it, whereas a fermion-to-qubit mapping returns a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), which has no concept of grouping.\n"
msgstr "Dala ng isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") na gate ang time evolution na $e^{-itH}$ ng buong operator. Isinusulat muli ng fermion-to-fermion synthesis ang gate na iyon bilang isang [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") ng mas maliliit na fermionic gate. Parehong nananatili sa fermionic space ang magkabilang panig ng pagsusulat muli, na siyang nagpapaiba rito sa fermion-to-qubit synthesis na kasunod: nananatili rito ang mga [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") ng operator (tingnan ang [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)), samantalang ang fermion-to-qubit mapping ay nagbabalik ng [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), na walang konsepto ng grouping.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two knobs select the method. `Evolution.synthesis` sets it on one gate, and the [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") transpiler pass sets it across a whole circuit. Both take an [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\"), the interface any such rewrite implements. The methods this package currently provides for an evolution are product formulas, which is what the rest of this guide uses: [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") for a first-order formula (the default) and [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") for a higher even order. Anything else implementing the interface is selected the same way, and the sections on the two knobs apply to it unchanged.\n"
msgstr "Dalawang setting ang pumipili ng pamamaraan. Itinatakda ito ng `Evolution.synthesis` sa isang gate, at itinatakda naman ito ng [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") na transpiler pass sa buong circuit. Parehong tumatanggap ng [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\"), ang interface na ipinapatupad ng anumang ganitong pagsusulat muli. Ang mga pamamaraang kasalukuyang inihahandog ng package na ito para sa isang evolution ay mga product formula, na siyang ginagamit sa natitirang bahagi ng gabay na ito: [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") para sa first-order na formula (ang default) at [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") para sa mas mataas na even order. Pinipili sa parehong paraan ang anumang iba pang nagpapatupad ng interface, at nalalapat nang walang pagbabago sa kanila ang mga seksyon tungkol sa dalawang setting.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  This fermion-to-fermion step is **optional**. An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate can go straight to the fermion-to-qubit stage, which maps and synthesizes it whole however many terms it holds. Splitting it first is a choice, made because the resulting gates are individually cheaper or because the split exposes structure that a later stage can use.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **Opsyonal** ang fermion-to-fermion na hakbang na ito. Maaaring dumiretso ang isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") na gate sa fermion-to-qubit na yugto, na nagma-map at nagsi-synthesize nito nang buo gaano man karami ang laman nitong term. Ang paghahati muna rito ay isang pagpili, na ginagawa dahil mas mura ang bawat nagreresultang gate o dahil inilalantad ng paghahati ang estrukturang magagamit ng susunod na yugto.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The two steps compose, so an evolution can end up approximated at either level, at both, or at neither. A product formula approximates unless its factors commute; a synthesis method need not approximate at all.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Nagko-compose ang dalawang hakbang, kaya ang isang evolution ay maaaring ma-approximate sa alinmang antas, sa pareho, o sa wala. Nag-a-approximate ang isang product formula maliban kung nagko-commute ang mga factor nito; hindi kailangang mag-approximate ang isang synthesis method.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Skipping this step does not have to mean losing the grouping entirely. Wrapping the mapper in [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\") maps the operator one group at a time and sums the results, so the mapped Pauli terms arrive grouped rather than interleaved. A qubit-side product formula synthesizes them in the order it receives, so commuting terms that end up adjacent can be scheduled together.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Hindi kailangang mangahulugan ang pagpapalampas sa hakbang na ito ng ganap na pagkawala ng grouping. Kapag binalot ang mapper sa [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\"), imamapa nito ang operator isang group sa bawat pagkakataon at isusuma ang mga resulta, kaya dumarating nang naka-group ang mga na-map na Pauli term imbes na magkakahalo. Sinisynthesize ng qubit-side na product formula ang mga ito ayon sa pagkakasunod na natanggap nito, kaya ang mga nagko-commute na term na nagkataong magkatabi ay maaaring i-schedule nang sabay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  On the Hamiltonian below that recovers the whole two-qubit depth benefit of splitting: 18 instead of 30, at an unchanged gate count. The difference is *where* the structure is expressed. Splitting in fermionic space makes each group a separate gate, which every later stage can see and act on; `group_wise` leaves one gate and only reorders the terms inside it, which is enough for scheduling but leaves nothing for a fermionic pass to work with. Use it when the evolution has to stay a single gate, and reach for a fermionic product formula otherwise.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Sa Hamiltonian sa ibaba, nababawi nito ang buong benepisyo sa two-qubit depth ng paghahati: 18 imbes na 30, na hindi nagbabago ang bilang ng gate. Ang pagkakaiba ay nasa *kung saan* ipinapahayag ang estruktura. Ang paghahati sa fermionic space ay ginagawang hiwalay na gate ang bawat group, na nakikita at magagamit ng bawat susunod na yugto; ang `group_wise` ay nag-iiwan ng isang gate at inaayos lang ang pagkakasunod ng mga term sa loob nito, na sapat para sa scheduling ngunit walang iniiwan para pagtrabahuhan ng isang fermionic pass. Gamitin ito kapag kailangang manatiling iisang gate ang evolution, at gumamit ng fermionic product formula sa iba pang kaso.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a grouped Hamiltonian {#build-a-grouped-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Bumuo ng grouped na Hamiltonian {#build-a-grouped-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both product formulas split an operator into factors, and for a grouped operator those factors are its groups. The grouping is therefore what determines both the cost and the accuracy of the result. Take a six-site Fermi-Hubbard chain, grouped the way its terms commute: the hopping terms on even bonds, the hopping terms on odd bonds, and the diagonal interaction.\n"
msgstr "Parehong hinahati ng dalawang product formula ang isang operator sa mga factor, at para sa isang grouped na operator, ang mga group nito ang mga factor na iyon. Kaya ang grouping ang nagtatakda ng parehong gastos at katumpakan ng resulta. Kumuha ng anim-na-site na Fermi-Hubbard chain, na naka-group ayon sa pagko-commute ng mga term nito: ang mga hopping term sa even bond, ang mga hopping term sa odd bond, at ang diagonal na interaksyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fifteen terms in three groups. Each hopping group pairs every term with its conjugate partner, which matters: a factor has to be Hermitian for its exponential to be unitary, and that does not follow from the sum being Hermitian. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") checks that convention rather than leaving it to inspection:\n"
msgstr "Labinlimang term sa tatlong group. Ipinapares ng bawat hopping group ang bawat term sa conjugate partner nito, na mahalaga: kailangang Hermitian ang isang factor para maging unitary ang exponential nito, at hindi iyon awtomatikong sumusunod sa pagiging Hermitian ng kabuuan. Sinusuri ng [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") ang convention na iyon imbes na iasa sa inspeksyon:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Separating $a^\\dagger_0 a_1$ from its partner $a^\\dagger_1 a_0$ would break it, and leaving the operator ungrouped has the same effect, since both formulas then split it *term by term* and a lone $a^\\dagger_i a_j$ is not Hermitian:\n"
msgstr "Masisira ito kapag pinaghiwalay ang $a^\\dagger_0 a_1$ mula sa partner nitong $a^\\dagger_1 a_0$, at ganoon din ang epekto ng pag-iwan sa operator na hindi naka-group, dahil hahatiin ito ng parehong formula *term por term* at hindi Hermitian ang nag-iisang $a^\\dagger_i a_j$:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Such a factor is a valid fermionic operator, and this package will build the gate for it, so nothing complains until the mapped operator reaches [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), which requires real coefficients and raises `ValueError: Operator contains complex coefficients, which are not supported`. Checking the grouping up front turns that late failure into an answer available before any circuit is built.\n"
msgstr "Ang ganitong factor ay isang balidong fermionic operator, at bubuuin ng package na ito ang gate para rito, kaya walang magrereklamo hanggang sa umabot ang na-map na operator sa [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), na nangangailangan ng mga real na coefficient at nagtataas ng `ValueError: Operator contains complex coefficients, which are not supported`. Ang pagsuri sa grouping nang maaga ay ginagawang sagot na makukuha bago pa buuin ang anumang circuit ang huling pagkabigong iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the method on one gate {#set-the-method-on-one-gate}"
msgstr "Itakda ang pamamaraan sa isang gate {#set-the-method-on-one-gate}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass a synthesis method to the gate, then decompose it. Each gate it emits comes back as its own [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate:\n"
msgstr "Magpasa ng synthesis method sa gate, pagkatapos ay i-decompose ito. Bawat gate na ibinubuga nito ay bumabalik bilang sarili nitong [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") na gate:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First order emits one factor per group. Order two emits the symmetric palindrome, so the two outer groups appear twice at half the time each, giving five. Four repetitions of that would give twenty, but each repetition ends on the same group the next one begins with. Those neighboring gates evolve under the same operator, so they are fused into one gate with the summed time, which saves one gate per seam. Pass `merge_adjacent=False` to keep the textbook sequence. Every order splits the operator the same way; what changes is the ordering of the factors and their evolution times, not the partition.\n"
msgstr "Ang first order ay naglalabas ng isang factor kada group. Ang order two ay naglalabas ng simetrikong palindrome, kaya lumalabas nang dalawang beses ang dalawang panlabas na group na may kalahating oras bawat isa, na nagbibigay ng lima. Ang apat na pag-ulit nito ay magbibigay ng dalawampu, ngunit bawat pag-ulit ay nagtatapos sa parehong group na pinagsisimulan ng susunod. Ang mga magkatabing gate na iyon ay nag-e-evolve sa ilalim ng parehong operator, kaya pinagsasama sila sa isang gate na may pinagsamang oras, na nakakatipid ng isang gate kada tahi. Ipasa ang `merge_adjacent=False` para panatilihin ang sunud-sunod na pagkakasunod sa aklat. Pareho ang paghahati ng bawat order sa operator; ang nagbabago ay ang pagkakasunod ng mga factor at ang evolution time nila, hindi ang partition.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The factors are marked `atomic`, so decomposing again leaves them in place rather than splitting them further. The decomposition has a fixed point, which is what makes it safe to call [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") repeatedly.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Minarkahan ang mga factor bilang `atomic`, kaya ang muling pag-decompose ay iiwan sila sa kinalalagyan nila imbes na hatiin pa. May fixed point ang decomposition, kaya ligtas na tawagin ang [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") nang paulit-ulit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the method for a whole pipeline {#set-the-method-for-a-whole-pipeline}"
msgstr "Itakda ang pamamaraan para sa buong pipeline {#set-the-method-for-a-whole-pipeline}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting `synthesis` per gate means threading the choice through everything that builds one, including [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") and [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\"), which construct their gates internally. The [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") pass applies one method to every [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") in a circuit instead, so the choice is made once for the pipeline. It is configured by gate name, the same way [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\") is, and a gate that is not named is left as it is:\n"
msgstr "Ang pagtatakda ng `synthesis` kada gate ay nangangahulugan ng pagpapasa ng pagpili sa lahat ng bumubuo nito, kasama ang [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") at [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\"), na bumubuo ng sarili nilang mga gate sa loob. Sa halip, ang [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") na pass ay naglalapat ng isang pamamaraan sa bawat [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") sa isang circuit, kaya isang beses lang ginagawa ang pagpili para sa pipeline. Kino-configure ito ayon sa pangalan ng gate, kapareho ng [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\"), at ang gate na hindi pinangalanan ay iniiwang kung ano ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the same count [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") gives for that method above. The [`MergeEvolutions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-evolutions#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeEvolutions \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeEvolutions\") pass applies the same fusion to neighboring gates that did not come from one synthesis, such as the seams between consecutive circuits. The pass carries the formula out itself, so no separate expansion step is needed, and running it twice changes nothing, since the factors it emits are `atomic` and so carry no definition of their own.\n"
msgstr "Ito ang parehong bilang na ibinibigay ng [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") para sa pamamaraang iyon sa itaas. Inilalapat ng [`MergeEvolutions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-evolutions#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeEvolutions \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeEvolutions\") na pass ang parehong pagsasama sa mga magkatabing gate na hindi nagmula sa iisang synthesis, tulad ng mga tahi sa pagitan ng sunud-sunod na circuit. Ang pass mismo ang nagsasagawa ng formula, kaya hindi na kailangan ng hiwalay na hakbang ng pagpapalawak, at ang pagpapatakbo nito nang dalawang beses ay walang binabago, dahil `atomic` ang mga factor na inilalabas nito at kaya wala silang sariling definition.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Tandaan\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Pass `apply=False` to only *select* the method and leave the expansion to something else, such as Qiskit’s [`Decompose`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Decompose) (naming the gate as `Decompose(\"Evolution\")` restricts it to the evolutions, leaving the other fermionic gates to their own synthesis plugins).\n"
msgstr "  Ipasa ang `apply=False` para *piliin* lang ang pamamaraan at ipaubaya ang pagpapalawak sa iba, tulad ng [`Decompose`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Decompose) ng Qiskit (ang pagpapangalan sa gate bilang `Decompose(\"Evolution\")` ay naglilimita rito sa mga evolution, at iniiwan ang iba pang fermionic gate sa sarili nilang synthesis plugin).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  This is useful to choose the method for a whole circuit up front while deferring the expansion to the point where it is wanted, for example to inspect the circuit first:\n"
msgstr "  Kapaki-pakinabang ito para piliin ang pamamaraan para sa buong circuit nang maaga habang ipinagpapaliban ang pagpapalawak hanggang sa puntong gusto ito, halimbawa para siyasatin muna ang circuit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Be aware of what an unexpanded gate does, though: it reaches the fermion-to-qubit stage whole, where it is mapped without `synthesis` being consulted. That makes for an easy mistake when comparing methods, because every one of them then produces identical output and the comparison silently measures nothing. On the Hamiltonian above, leaving the order-two gate unexpanded collapses the much larger circuit below to the cost of a single mapped evolution, no matter which method was selected.\n"
msgstr "  Gayunpaman, tandaan kung ano ang ginagawa ng hindi pa napapalawak na gate: umaabot ito nang buo sa fermion-to-qubit na yugto, kung saan ito ime-map nang hindi kinukonsulta ang `synthesis`. Madali itong pagkakamali kapag nagkukumpara ng mga pamamaraan, dahil lahat sila ay gumagawa ng magkakaparehong output at ang paghahambing ay tahimik na walang nasusukat. Sa Hamiltonian sa itaas, ang pag-iwan sa order-two na gate na hindi napapalawak ay nagpapabagsak sa mas malaking circuit sa ibaba hanggang sa gastos ng iisang na-map na evolution, anuman ang napiling pamamaraan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure the payoff {#measure-the-payoff}"
msgstr "Sukatin ang kapalit {#measure-the-payoff}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A higher order costs depth, so the question is not whether it is more accurate but whether it is more accurate *per gate*. Two numbers are needed per method: the error of the state it produces, and the two-qubit cost of the circuit that produced it.\n"
msgstr "Nagkakahalaga ng depth ang mas mataas na order, kaya ang tanong ay hindi kung mas tumpak ito kundi kung mas tumpak ba ito *kada gate*. Dalawang numero ang kailangan kada pamamaraan: ang error ng state na nabubuo nito, at ang two-qubit na gastos ng circuit na lumikha nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The error is measured with [ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/), which simulates a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") **directly** (see [How this package relates to ffsim](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation)). No fermion-to-qubit mapping is involved, so the comparison isolates the fermionic product formula from anything the mapping or the qubit-side synthesis might contribute. It also works in the fixed-particle-number sector, which is both smaller than the full $2^N$ space and the space the evolution actually stays in.\n"
msgstr "Sinusukat ang error gamit ang [ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/), na **direktang** nagsi-simulate ng isang [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") (tingnan ang [How this package relates to ffsim](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation)). Walang fermion-to-qubit mapping na kasangkot, kaya inihihiwalay ng paghahambing ang fermionic product formula sa anumang maidudulot ng mapping o ng qubit-side synthesis. Gumagana rin ito sa fixed-particle-number sector, na parehong mas maliit kaysa sa buong $2^N$ na espasyo at ang espasyong talagang kinalalagyan ng evolution.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two-qubit cost is left out of that table on purpose. It depends on the qubit-side synthesis Qiskit selects, which improves between releases, so the numbers printed here would be a snapshot rather than a property of the product formula. The figure below plots them instead, and what the comparison rests on is asserted as a relation:\n"
msgstr "Sinadyang hindi isama sa talahanayang iyon ang two-qubit na gastos. Nakadepende ito sa qubit-side synthesis na pinipili ng Qiskit, na bumubuti sa pagitan ng mga release, kaya ang mga numerong ipi-print dito ay magiging snapshot lang at hindi katangian ng product formula. Ipinapakita sila sa halip ng figure sa ibaba, at ang pinagbabatayan ng paghahambing ay ina-assert bilang isang relasyon:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Grouped bars of CX count and depth per method, with order two at four repetitions clearly shorter than order one at ten.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/fermionic_synthesis-8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Grouped bars of CX count and depth per method, with order two at four repetitions clearly shorter than order one at ten.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/fermionic_synthesis-8.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the last two methods together, because they are the comparison that matters. Order two with four repetitions is roughly ten times more accurate than order one with ten, and it gets there with fewer entangling gates rather than more, as the figure shows. Spending a gate budget on a higher order beats spending it on more first-order steps here.\n"
msgstr "Basahin nang magkasama ang huling dalawang pamamaraan, dahil iyon ang paghahambing na mahalaga. Ang order two na may apat na pag-ulit ay humigit-kumulang sampung beses na mas tumpak kaysa sa order one na may sampu, at narating nito iyon na may mas kaunti, hindi mas marami, na entangling gate, gaya ng ipinapakita ng figure. Sa kasong ito, mas mainam na gugulin ang gate budget sa mas mataas na order kaysa sa mas maraming first-order na step.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That result is not universal. Increasing [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.reps\") and increasing [`order`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.order \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.order\") reduce the error at different rates for the same kind of cost, and which wins depends on the operator and on the time being evolved. The two rows above are how to find out for a given problem.\n"
msgstr "Hindi pangkalahatan ang resultang iyon. Ang pagtaas ng [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.reps\") at ang pagtaas ng [`order`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.order \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.order\") ay nagbabawas ng error sa magkaibang bilis para sa parehong uri ng gastos, at nakadepende sa operator at sa oras na ie-evolve kung alin ang mananalo. Ang dalawang hanay sa itaas ang paraan para malaman ito para sa isang partikular na problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The fermionic formula composes with the one chosen for the fermion-to-qubit stage (see [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\")). Where both approximate, the accuracy of the result is governed by the weaker of the two, so raising the order here while the qubit-side formula stays first-order buys little.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Nagko-compose ang fermionic formula sa pinili para sa fermion-to-qubit na yugto (tingnan ang [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\")). Kung pareho silang nag-a-approximate, ang katumpakan ng resulta ay nakadepende sa mas mahina sa dalawa, kaya kaunti lang ang makukuha sa pagtataas ng order dito habang first-order pa rin ang qubit-side na formula.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Restrict the pass to the gates that benefit {#restrict-the-pass-to-the-gates-that-benefit}"
msgstr "Limitahan ang pass sa mga gate na makikinabang {#restrict-the-pass-to-the-gates-that-benefit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A higher order only helps when the factors do not commute. If they all commute, the first-order formula is already exact and the extra factors are pure overhead. A purely diagonal operator makes that concrete, since number operators commute with each other:\n"
msgstr "Nakakatulong lang ang mas mataas na order kapag hindi nagko-commute ang mga factor. Kung lahat sila ay nagko-commute, eksakto na ang first-order na formula at purong overhead na ang mga dagdag na factor. Ginagawang kongkreto ito ng isang puro diagonal na operator, dahil nagko-commute ang mga number operator sa isa't isa:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both circuits are exact, so the second spends 80% more entangling gates for nothing. The diagonal Coulomb operators of a [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") have this shape, which is why [`F2FSynthesis.filter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis.filter \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis.filter\") exists: it takes a predicate over the [`DAGOpNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.dagcircuit.DAGOpNode) and leaves the rejected gates untouched, so one pass can raise the order on the gates that benefit and leave the rest at first order.\n"
msgstr "Parehong eksakto ang dalawang circuit, kaya ang pangalawa ay gumagastos ng 80% na mas maraming entangling gate nang walang napapala. Ganito ang hugis ng mga diagonal na Coulomb operator ng isang [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\"), kaya umiiral ang [`F2FSynthesis.filter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis.filter \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis.filter\"): kumukuha ito ng predicate sa [`DAGOpNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.dagcircuit.DAGOpNode) at hindi ginagalaw ang mga tinanggihang gate, kaya maaaring itaas ng isang pass ang order sa mga gate na makikinabang at iwanan ang iba sa first order.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A circuit holding both kinds of evolution shows what that saves. The predicate below accepts a gate only when its operator moves particles between modes, which is exactly when the groups fail to commute and a higher order has something to buy:\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng isang circuit na may parehong uri ng evolution kung gaano ang natitipid nito. Tinatanggap lang ng predicate sa ibaba ang isang gate kapag naglilipat ng mga particle sa pagitan ng mga mode ang operator nito, na siyang eksaktong sandali kung kailan hindi nagko-commute ang mga group at may mapapala ang mas mataas na order:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The gates the filter saves are exactly the ones order two spent on the diagonal evolution, which the diagonal comparison above prices at eight (18 against 10). They bought nothing there, because that evolution is already exact at first order, so dropping them costs no accuracy.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga gate na natitipid ng filter ay eksaktong ang mga ginastos ng order two sa diagonal na evolution, na ayon sa diagonal na paghahambing sa itaas ay may halagang walo (18 kumpara sa 10). Wala silang naibigay doon, dahil eksakto na ang evolution na iyon sa first order, kaya ang pag-alis sa kanila ay walang nawawalang katumpakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Compare the two order-two circuits with each other, not against the unexpanded one. Leaving both gates unexpanded sends each to the fermion-to-qubit stage whole, which is the mistake the `apply=False` note above describes: it can land on the same entangling-gate count as the filtered circuit while being a different circuit at a different depth, so reading the filter’s benefit off that number measures nothing.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ihambing ang dalawang order-two na circuit sa isa't isa, hindi sa hindi pa napapalawak. Ang pag-iwan sa dalawang gate na hindi napapalawak ay nagpapadala sa bawat isa sa fermion-to-qubit na yugto nang buo, na siyang pagkakamaling inilalarawan ng tala tungkol sa `apply=False` sa itaas: maaari itong mauwi sa parehong bilang ng entangling gate gaya ng na-filter na circuit habang ibang circuit na may ibang depth, kaya ang pagbasa ng benepisyo ng filter mula sa numerong iyon ay walang nasusukat.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Caution\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Neither knob verifies that the factors are Hermitian, and an incorrectly grouped operator can look *better* at an even order than at first order while still being wrong, because the symmetrization partially cancels the error. Group conjugate partners together, as `fermi_hubbard_chain` above does.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Babala\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Hindi bine-verify ng alinmang setting na Hermitian ang mga factor, at ang maling naka-group na operator ay maaaring magmukhang *mas maganda* sa even order kaysa sa first order habang mali pa rin, dahil bahagyang binubura ng symmetrization ang error. Pagsamahin ang mga conjugate partner, gaya ng ginagawa ng `fermi_hubbard_chain` sa itaas.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

